            <ArticleTitle>A two-photon fluorescent probe for ratiometric imaging of endogenous hypochlorous acid in live cells and tissues.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10800-10803</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc05834a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A fluorescent probe that enables ratiometric imaging of endogenous hypochlorous acid (HOCl) in cells and tissues by two-photon microscopy is developed based on a red-emitting acetyl-benzocoumarin (AcBC) dye. An oxathiolane group in the probe reacts with HOCl to generate the AcBC dye, which involves a ratiometric fluorescence change only toward HOCl along with high sensitivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
